From d3dd55e5c8ba260939da7740b8038d483adab412 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wilbolu <wilbolu@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:48:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix(capture): support slotted request KV admission state

The pinned ReqKvInfo is a slotted dataclass, so vars(req.kv) fails before plugin prepare and reserve. Snapshot declared dataclass fields without deep-copying tensor/resource handles and restore each field on the existing KV object. Keep namespace/test-double compatibility without relying on a production __dict__.

Preserve the concrete admission failure and HTTP status in scheduler abort output, and log native local-phase tracebacks before TP error strings are exchanged. Regression executes actual pinned Req constructor, ReqKvInfo decorators, native PrefillBudget and scheduler rejection method bodies.

Validation: 4 new actual-Req CPU regressions, 21 existing admission/control contracts, 4 GDN wrapper contracts and 9 independent actual-method/CPU-allocator cases pass using system Python with CUDA hidden. No GPU, venv or integration checkout was changed; real capture smoke rerun remains pending validation ownership.
